verses.tf_bn:
① **«هُوَ الَّذِیْ بَعَثَ فِی الْاُمِّیّٖنَ رَسُوْلًا مِّنْهُمْ»** — তিনিই সেই দয়াময় রব, যিনি অক্ষরজ্ঞানহীন উম্মী জাতি আরবদের মধ্য থেকেই তাদেরই স্বগোত্রীয় এক মহামান্বিত রাসুল—সাইয়্যিদুনা মুহাম্মাদ মুস্তফা ﷺ-কে সমগ্র মানবজাতির মুক্তির দিশারি হিসেবে মبعূস করেছেন।
② **«یَتْلُوْا عَلَیْهِمْ اٰیٰتِهٖ»** — যাঁর প্রথম মৌলিক দায়িত্ব হলো, তিনি তাদের সামনে আল্লাহ তাআলার আসমানি আয়াতসমূহ নিখুঁতভাবে তিলাওয়াত করে শোনান;
③ **«وَیُزَكِّیْهِمْ»** — এবং তিনি তাঁদের আত্মিক ও বাতিনি পরিচ্ছন্নতা সাধন (তাজকিয়ায়ে নফস) করেন—শিরক, কুফর, অহংকার ও চারিত্রিক যাবতীয় কলুষতা থেকে তাঁদের অন্তরকে নিষ্কলুষ স্বর্ণের ন্যায় খাঁটি বানিয়ে দেন;
④ **«وَیُعَلِّمُهُمُ الْكِتٰبَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ»** — এবং তিনি তাঁদেরকে আল্লাহর পবিত্র কিতাবের নিগূঢ় অর্থ ও শরিয়তের সুক্ষ্ম প্রজ্ঞা ও হিকমত (সুন্নাহর বিধানাবলি) শিক্ষা দান করেন;
⑤ **«وَاِنْ كَانُوْا مِنْ قَبْلُ لَفِیْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِیْنٍ»** — অথচ এই মহান রাসুল ﷺ-এর শুভাগমনের পূর্বে তারা নিশ্চিতভাবেই নিমজ্জিত ছিল পৌত্তলিকতা, অজ্ঞতা ও সুস্পষ্ট পথভ্রষ্টতার অতল গহ্বরে। রাসুলুল্লাহ ﷺ-এর শুভাগমন মানবজাতির ইতিহাসে সর্বশ্রেষ্ঠ ঐশী অনুগ্রহ।

verses.tf_en:
① **«هُوَ الَّذِیْ بَعَثَ فِی الْاُمِّیّٖنَ رَسُوْلًا مِّنْهُمْ»** (It is He Who has sent among the unlettered people a Noble Messenger from themselves,) — He is the Boundlessly Gracious Lord Who raised up among the unlettered Arabs (*al-Ummiyyeen*) a magnificent, illustrious Messenger from their own midst—our Master Muhammad al-Mustafa ﷺ—as the universal savior for all mankind;
② **«یَتْلُوْا عَلَیْهِمْ اٰیٰتِهٖ»** (Who recites His verses to them) — Whose foundational divine commission is to recite unto them the living, miraculous verses of Allah's Holy Qur'an;
③ **«وَیُزَكِّیْهِمْ»** (And purifies them,) — And to perform their inward and spiritual purification (*Tazkiyah*), cleansing their hearts from the filth of polytheism, arrogance, moral vices, and spiritual maladies, elevating them into luminous paragons of virtue;
④ **«وَیُعَلِّمُهُمُ الْكِتٰبَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ»** (And bestows them the knowledge of the Book and wisdom;) — And to instruct them in the esoteric and exoteric meanings of the Divine Book and deep prophetic wisdom (*al-Hikmah*, the Sunnah and Sacred Jurisprudence);
⑤ **«وَاِنْ كَانُوْا مِنْ قَبْلُ لَفِیْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِیْنٍ»** (And indeed before this, they were in open error.) — Although prior to his radiant advent, they were plunged headlong into the darkest abysses of idol worship, lawlessness, and manifest misguidance! The advent of the Holy Prophet ﷺ is the crowning mercy of Allah upon humanity.

① **«مَثَلُ الَّذِیْنَ حُمِّلُوا التَّوْرٰىةَ ثُمَّ لَمْ یَحْمِلُوْهَا كَمَثَلِ الْحِمَارِ یَحْمِلُ اَسْفَارًا»** (The example of those who were entrusted with the Taurat, and did not carry out its commands, is like the donkey carrying books;) — The similitude of the Jewish rabbis and scholars who were entrusted with the sacred guardianship of the Torah and commanded to uphold its prophecies, yet failed to act upon its teachings and stubbornly denied the Final Prophet ﷺ clearly foretold therein, is like that of a beast of burden carrying a heavy load of scholarly volumes on its back! Just as a donkey derives nothing from the precious wisdom on its back except physical exhaustion, so too these scholars gained nothing from their sacred scripture except spiritual ruin;
② **«بِئْسَ مَثَلُ الْقَوْمِ الَّذِیْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰیٰتِ اللّٰهِ»** (What a wretched example is of the people who denied the signs of Allah;) — How utterly wretched and disgraceful is the parable of that people who arrogantly rejected the clear verses, signs, and prophecies of Allah!;
③ **«وَاللّٰهُ لَا یَهْدِی الْقَوْمَ الظّٰلِمِیْنَ»** (And Allah does not guide the unjust.) — And Allah does not guide a stubborn, self-deluded, and tyrannical people (*al-Qawm az-Zalimeen*).

① **«یٰۤاَیُّهَا الَّذِیْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِذَا نُوْدِیَ لِلصَّلٰوةِ مِنْ یَّوْمِ الْجُمُعَةِ فَاسْعَوْا اِلٰی ذِكْرِ اللّٰهِ»** (O People who Believe! When the call for prayer is given on (Friday) the day of congregation, rush towards the remembrance of Allah) — This establishes the sacred obligation of the Friday Congregational Prayer (*Salat al-Jumu'ah*): O you who believe! When the formal call to prayer (*Adhan*) is sounded on Friday—specifically the second Adhan proclaimed before the sermon (*Khutbah*)—hasten eagerly and mindfully to the remembrance of Allah, which encompasses attentive listening to the Khutbah and performing the congregational prayer;
② **«وَذَرُوا الْبَیْعَ»** (And stop buying and selling;) — And immediately suspend, forsake, and cease all trade, commercial transactions, and worldly business, for engaging in commerce during this sacred window is strictly prohibited (*Haram*);
③ **«ذٰلِكُمْ خَیْرٌ لَّكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَ»** (This is better for you if you understand.) — This dedication to the divine assembly is immeasurably superior and far more lucrative for your eternal destiny and spiritual welfare than all the commercial profits of the globe, if you truly possess understanding!

① **«وَاِذَا رَاَوْا تِجَارَةً اَوْ لَهْوَا انْفَضُّوْۤا اِلَیْهَا وَتَرَكُوْكَ قَاۤئِمًا»** (And when they see some trade or sport, they move towards it and leave you standing delivering the sermon;) — *Occasion of Revelation (Sabab an-Nuzul):* During a severe drought and famine in Madinah, a merchant caravan laden with grain and beating welcoming drums arrived from Syria precisely while the Holy Prophet ﷺ was delivering the Friday sermon from the pulpit; out of urgent need and excitement, a group of congregation members rushed toward the market, leaving the Holy Prophet ﷺ standing upon the Minbar with only twelve steadfast Sahabah (including Abu Bakr and 'Umar, radiyallahu 'anhuma) remaining fixed in reverent devotion. Thereupon, Allah gently admonished the believers concerning the supreme etiquette of the Prophet's assembly;
② **«قُلْ مَا عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ خَیْرٌ مِّنَ اللَّهْوِ وَمِنَ التِّجَارَةِ»** (Proclaim, “That which is with Allah, is better than sport and trade;) — Proclaim unto them, O Messenger ﷺ: 'That celestial reward, divine contentment, and eternal bliss which resides with Allah in the presence of His Messenger is infinitely superior and more enduring than any fleeting amusement or commercial gain!';
③ **«وَاللّٰهُ خَیْرُ الرّٰزِقِیْنَ»** (And the sustenance of Allah is the best.”) — And Allah alone is the Best of all sustainers; true abundance and blessings flow not through commercial anxiety, but through sincere obedience to Allah and veneration of His Beloved Messenger ﷺ! [With this luminous verse, Surah Al-Jumu'ah is completed in its entirety].
